---
/**
 * Presents a source-limited artist introduction and the retained visual identity.
 *
 * Dependencies: BaseLayout and reviewed public links.
 * Depended on by: Footer and reference routes.
 * Why this exists: Visitors need artist context without fabricated biography or credentials.
 */
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ArtistPhotos from "../components/ArtistPhotos.astro";
import { site } from "../content";
---

<BaseLayout title="About Justin LeBlanc" canonicalPath="/about/">
  <section class="page-intro">
    <div class="page-shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Singer · guitarist · event inquiry</p>
      <h1>Justin LeBlanc, in his own blue.</h1>
      <p>
        This redesign keeps the electric-blue guitar portrait and direct personal tone of Justin's
        current site while making private-event planning easier to understand.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <ArtistPhotos variant="portrait" />
  <section class="section page-shell split-section">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What is verified here</h2>
      <p>
        Justin's current website says he is booking private events in Houston and beyond. His public
        Instagram and YouTube identities use the handle <strong>@jus10sense</strong> and are linked
        from that site.
      </p>
      <p>
        The demo does not add a repertoire, client list, award, current package, review, or technical
        capability without an approved source. Historical profiles and social posts are not treated
        as proof of today's booking offer.
      </p>
      <a class="button" href="/plan-your-event/">Tell Justin about your event</a>
    </div>
    <aside class="source-card">
      <p class="eyebrow">Explore the public identity</p>
      <h3>Sources, not invented biography.</h3>
      <p>Use Justin's own public pages for music and current updates.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href={site.currentSite} rel="external">Current website →</a><br />
      <a class="text-link" href={site.instagram} rel="external">Instagram →</a><br />
      <a class="text-link" href={site.youtube} rel="external">YouTube →</a>
    </aside>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
